think Design: paint_checkerboard(target,x,y,w,h,cell,a,b) routes cell (col,row) to a color by (col+row) parity; a boundary cell the cell size does not divide is CLIPPED to the edge (ceiling-division cell count) so the board always tiles exactly. paint_alpha_ground is the one-call convenience with the conventional light/white shades and cell 8.
